{"title":"2000 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three squares with the same centre and corresponding parallel sides are drawn. The distance between the sides of successive squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the side length of the largest square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, as shown. What is the perimeter of the smallest square?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f208f9aee585982e66a711b006707072889345be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 40 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 100 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 64 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the perimeter of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a>, we can find the side length of the small square, and then multiply it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the small square. We also know that distance between the sides of successive squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can see that the side length of the full square is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73b5d8ed5348285f70a3bcecda691a173d4510db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 3 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />, allowing us to set up an equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b85b3e14a8e328f75eb4f42b1c82f198aefe2815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 3 \\times 4 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a7c69529df8b897ebd2f3eac4805f2770505d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 12 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b01e2d02cb8d2c58e34793ad74bd04a71a362bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 22 - 12 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the perimeter, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0d3c370c731518fc1bf4e4c9a570c8c0d189827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal\">2000 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center